1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,500
<i>Solar flare activity has increased across
space lanes 5,5,6. All commercial flights are...</i>

2
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:16,300
<font face="Monotype Corsiva" color=#D900D9"> © anoXmous </ font>
<font face="Monotype Corsiva" color=#D900D9"> @ http://thepiratebay.sx/user/Zen_Bud </font>

3
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:31,500
So, it's 200,000. It's a spaceship...
No, a space station, and, er...

4
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,200
- Try that gate over there.
- 200,000?

5
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,600
- 200,000.
- Nice.

6
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,700
Adam! Out you come.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,600
- Oh, my God!
- Don't worry. You'll get used to it.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,600
- Where are we?
- Good question. Let's see.

9
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:53,700
Judging by the architecture, I'd say we're
around the year 200,000, and if you listen...

10
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,200
Engines. We're in a space station.

11
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:03,400
Yeah, definitely a space station. It's a bit warm in here.
They could turn the heating down.

12
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,500
Tell you what - let's try that gate.
Come on.

13
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,700
Here we go.

14
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,700
And this is...

15
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,300
I'll let the Doctor describe it.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,300
The Fourth Great and Bountiful Human Empire. There it is
- Planet Earth at its height.

17
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:35,100
Covered with mega-cities, five moons,
population 96 billion.

18
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:41,300
The hub of a galactic domain stretching
across a million planets, a million species,

19
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,700
with mankind right in the middle.

20
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,200
He's your boyfriend (!)

21
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,800
Not any more.

22
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,900
Come on, Adam. Open your mind.
You'll like this - fantastic period of history.

23
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:43,400
The human race at its most intelligent -
art, politics, fine food, good manners...

24
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,700
Out the way!

25
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,900
- Is somebody there? That's great.
- What do you want, love?

26
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,800
One at a time. What was it? Kronkburger
with cheese, kronkburger with pajatos.

27
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:03,700
Do you want a drink? Oi! Stop pushing!

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,800
Get back! I said, back!

29
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,500
- Fine cuisine?
- My watch must be wrong.

30
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:15,400
- No, it's fine. It's weird.
- Your history's not as good as you thought.

31
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:18,000
- It's perfect.
- Obviously not.

32
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:22,300
What about the millions of planets
and species? Where are they?

33
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,500
That is a good question.

34
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:28,800
- Adam, me old mate. You must be starving.
- No, I'm a bit timesick.

35
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:32,000
You need some grub.
How much is a kronkburger?

36
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,900
Two credits twenty, sweetheart.
Now, join the queue!

37
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:39,400
We need money. Let's use a cashpoint.

38
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:51,800
- Pocket money. Don't spend it all on sweets.
- How does it work?

39
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:58,500
Go and find out. Stop nagging me! Time travel's
like visiting Paris. Don't just read a guidebook.

40
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:04,000
Throw yourself in - eat the food, get charged
double and kiss complete strangers...

41
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,700
Or is that just me?

42
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,300
Stop asking questions. Go and do it!

43
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:13,000
- Off you go. Your first date (!)
- You're gonna get a smack, you are!

44
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:21,100
This is gonna sound daft,
but can you tell me where I am?

45
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,300
- Floor 139.
- Could they write it any bigger (?)

46
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,700
- Floor 139 of what?
- Must have been some party!

47
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:31,100
- You're on Satellite Five.
- What's that?

48
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:34,700
- How could you not know where you are?
- I'm stupid!

49
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,700
Wait a minute. Are you a test?
Some sort of management test kind of thing?

50
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:42,600
You've got me. You're too clever for me.

51
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,600
We were warned about
this in basic training.

52
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,800
Workers have to be versed
in company promotion.

53
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:52,900
Right. Fire away.
If it gets me to Floor 500,

54
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:56,300
- I'll do anything.
- What happens on Floor 500?

55
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,000
The walls are made of gold!

56
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,300
And you should know, Mr Management!

57
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:07,200
So, this is what we do.

58
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:13,700
Latest news - sandstorms
on the New Venus Archipelago, 200 dead.

59
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:19,500
The Glasgow water riots into their third day.
Space lane 77 closed by sunspot activity.

60
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,300
And the Face of Boe
has just announced he's pregnant.

61
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,500
You broadcast the news.

62
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:30,300
We ARE the news. We're the journalists.

63
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:36,900
We write it, package it and sell it.
600 channels broadcasting out of Satellite Five.

64
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,200
Something... is wrong.

65
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,300
Something fictional.

66
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,700
Those people.

67
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,900
<i>Nothing happens in the whole empire
without it going through us.</i>

68
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,800
Security check.

69
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,200
Go deep.

70
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:08,300
<i>Staff are reminded that the canteen
area operates a self-cleaning table system.</i>

71
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:12,800
Try this. It's called Zaffic.
It's like a Slush Puppy.

72
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,800
What flavour?

73
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:18,700
Sort of beef.

74
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,900
Oh, my God!

75
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:28,900
It's like everything's gone -
home, family - everything.

76
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:33,600
This helps. The Doctor gave it a top-up.

77
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:36,500
- Who's back home? Your mum and dad?
- Yeah.

78
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:41,700
- Phone 'em up.
- But that's 198,000 years ago.

79
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,700
Honestly. Try it. Go on.

80
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:48,000
- Is there a code for Planet Earth?
- Just dial!

81
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:58,500
<i>- Sorry we're not in.
- Please leave a message. Thanks.</i>

82
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,600
Hi. It's me.

83
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,600
<i>I've sort of gone travelling.</i>

84
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:12,800
<i>I met these people and we're
travelling together.</i>

85
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:18,300
I'm fine, and I'll call you later.
Love you. Bye.

86
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:21,900
That is so...

87
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,600
Oi, Mutt and Jeff! Over here.

88
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:41,800
<i>- Security check cleared.
- No. Something's wrong.</i>

89
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,700
I can taste it.

90
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:49,700
A tiny little shift in the information.

91
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,800
Someone down there shouldn't be here.

92
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,600
Double-check. Triple-check.

93
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,500
Follow them.

94
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:04,400
Now, everybody behave.
We have a management inspection.

95
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:08,500
- How do you want it, by the book?
- Right from scratch, thanks.

96
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:12,500
OK, so, ladies, gentlemen,
multisex, undecided or robot,

97
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:15,500
my name is Cathica Santini Khadeni.

98
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:21,100
That's Cathica with a C, in case you want to
write to Floor 500 praising me - please do!

99
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:25,700
Feel free to ask questions.
The process of news-gathering

100
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,900
must open, honest and beyond bias.

101
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:34,000
- That's company policy.
- Actually, it's the law.

102
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:40,400
Thank you, Suki. OK, keep it calm.
Don't show off for the guests.

103
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:43,000
Here we go.

104
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,200
And...

105
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,700
engage safety.

106
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,800
And three... two...

107
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,400
and spike.

108
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,200
Compressed information, streaming into her.

109
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:22,300
Reports from every city,
every country, every planet,

110
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:25,400
and they all get packaged inside her head.

111
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:29,300
She becomes part of the software.
Her brain IS the computer.

112
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:34,100
- If it goes through her, she must be a genius.
- She wouldn't remember it.

113
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,000
There's too much. Her head would blow up.

114
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:41,200
The brain's the processor.
Soon as it closes, she forgets.

115
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,400
What about all these people?

116
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:49,900
They've got tiny chips in their head, connecting
them to her. They transmit 600 channels.

117
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:54,400
Every single fact in the Empire
beams out of this place.

118
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,300
Now, that's what I call power.

119
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,900
<i>- Analysis confirmed.
- Security breach.</i>

120
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,800
I knew it!

121
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:08,100
Which one? It's someone inside that room.
Which one?

122
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,200
<i>Isolating breach.</i>

123
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:17,200
Come on. Show me. Who is it?

124
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,700
<i>- Are you OK?
- I can see her brain.</i>

125
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:26,700
- Do you want to get out?
- No. This technology, it's amazing.

126
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,100
This technology's wrong.

127
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,900
Trouble?

128
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,800
Oh, yeah.

129
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:43,600
That's it! Oh, yes! She's the liar.

130
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,800
Intercept and scan.

131
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,400
Gotcha!

132
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:58,000
Suki! I wasn't even halfway.
What was that for?

133
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,800
- Sorry. It must have been a glitch.
- Oh!

134
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:06,900
Her information's been tampered with.
There's a second biography hidden underneath.

135
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,700
Absolutely, sir.

136
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:15,600
Her data was encrypted, so there was no way
we could have found her sooner.

137
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,300
Sorry, sir.

138
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:21,300
Absolutely.

139
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,800
Get her up here. Now.

140
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,900
<i>Promotion!</i>

141
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,200
Come on! This is it. Come on!

142
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:31,900
Oh, my God. Make it me.

143
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,400
Come on. Say my name.

144
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,600
Say my name!

145
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:41,700
<i>Promotion for Suki Macrae Cantrell.</i>

146
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:45,100
<i>- Proceed to Floor 500.
- I don't believe it!</i>

147
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:47,800
Floor 500!

148
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:50,900
How the hell did you manage that?
I'm above you!

149
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:54,400
I don't know.
I just applied on the off chance.

150
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:56,800
And they've said yes!

151
00:11:57,100 --> 00:12:01,100
It's so not fair! I've been applying
to Floor 500 for three years!

152
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,800
What's Floor 500?

153
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:05,700
The walls are made of gold.

154
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,900
Cathica, I'm gonna miss you!

155
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:13,200
- Floor 500! Thank you!
- I didn't do anything.

156
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:17,400
- Well, you're my lucky charm!
- All right. I'll hug anyone.

157
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:22,700
- Come on. It's not that bad.
- What, with the head thing?

158
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,600
- Well, she's closed it now.
- Yeah, but it...

159
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:31,300
It's everything. It freaks me out.

160
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,600
I just need to... If I could just...

161
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:39,900
cool down. Sort of acclimatise.
- How do you mean?

162
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:45,900
Maybe I could sit on the observation deck.
Would that be all right?

163
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:50,900
Soak it in, you know.
Pretend I'm a citizen of the year 200,000.

164
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,500
Do you want me to come with you?

165
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,900
No, no. You stick with the Doctor.

166
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,600
You'd rather be with him.

167
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,900
It's gonna take a better man than me
to get between you two.

168
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:13,800
- Anyway, I'll be on the deck.
- Here you go. Take the Tardis key.

169
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,500
Just in case it gets a bit too much.

170
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:19,100
Yeah, like it's not weird in there (!)

171
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,400
I've got to go.
I can't keep them waiting. I'm sorry!

172
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,500
Say goodbye to Steve for me.

173
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,900
Bye!

174
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,100
Good riddance!

175
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:47,100
- You're talking like you'll never see her again.
- We won't.

176
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:50,400
Once you go to Floor 500,
you never come back.

177
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,100
Have you ever been up there?

178
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:06,800
I can't. The key for the lift
only comes with promotion.

179
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:09,800
No one gets to 500 except
for the chosen few.

180
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,700
Agh!

181
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:00,400
- Who are you?
- I'm the Editor.

182
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:04,300
What's happening?

183
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:07,300
There are bodies out there.
What's going on?

184
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:11,100
While we're asking questions,
please confirm your name.

185
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:15,400
<i>My name is Suki Macrae Cantrell.</i>

186
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:18,100
<i>I was born 199'89</i>

187
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:21,300
<i>- in the Independent Republic of Morocco.
- Liar!</i>

188
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:27,400
<i>Hobbies include reading and archaeology.
 I'm not an expert, I just like digging.</i>

189
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,100
Liar!

190
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:34,100
<i>I want to work for Satellite Five
because my sister can't afford university</i>

191
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:37,100
<i>- and the pay scheme is really good.
- Liar!</i>

192
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,100
Let's look at the facts, shall we?

193
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:46,200
Ah, hidden behind a genetic graft,
but that's still you.

194
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:51,400
Eva Saint Julienne - last surviving
member of the Freedom Fifteen.

195
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:56,600
- Self-declared anarchist, is that right?
- Who controls Satellite Five?

196
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,400
There's the truth!

197
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:13,300
The Freedom Foundation has been
monitoring Satellite Five's transmissions.

198
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,900
The facts are being manipulated.

199
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:20,000
- You are lying to the people.
- Ooh, I love it. Say it again!

200
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,400
This whole system is corrupt.

201
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,900
Who do you represent?

202
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:30,400
I am merely a humble slave.
I answer to the Editor-in-chief.

203
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:37,400
- Who is he? Where is he?
- He oversees everything. Literally everything.

204
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:42,200
If you don't mind,
I'm going to have to refer this upwards.

205
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:49,700
- What is that?
- Your boss.

206
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
This has always been your boss -
since the day you were born.

207
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,900
Agh!

208
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,800
Give me access.

209
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:25,000
Give me...

210
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:29,200
I can learn anything!

211
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:38,400
Let's try computers.

212
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:44,000
From the 21st century to the present day,
give me the history of the microprocessor.

213
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,900
Oh, my God!

214
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,300
We only get 20 minutes' maintenance.

215
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:56,500
- Give it a rest!
- You've never been to another floor?

216
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:03,500
I went to Floor 16 when I first arrived. That's Medical.
I got my head done. Then I came here.

217
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:07,600
Satellite Five. We work,
eat and sleep on the same floor.

218
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:12,700
- You're not Management, are you?
- At last! She's clever!

219
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,200
- Well, whatever it is, I don't know anything.
- Don't you ask?

220
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:20,100
- Why would I?
- You're a journalist!

221
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:24,300
- Why is all the crew human?
- What's that got to do with anything?

222
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:29,400
- There's no aliens on board. Why?
- I dunno. They're not banned or anything.

223
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,500
Then where are they?

224
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:36,700
I suppose Immigration's tightened up
because of the threats.

225
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:39,600
- What threats?
- I dunno.

226
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:45,400
All of them. Usual stuff. And the price of
spacewarp doubled, so that kept visitors away.

227
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:50,600
And the government on Chavic Fice
collapsed, so that lot stopped coming.

228
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:52,700
Just lots of little reasons.

229
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,200
Adding up to one big fact,
and you didn't even notice.

230
00:20:56,600 --> 00:21:01,400
If there was a conspiracy, Satellite Five
would have seen it. We see everything.

231
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:05,100
This society's the wrong shape.
Even the technology.

232
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:10,200
- It's cutting edge!
- It's backwards. There's a door in your head!

233
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:15,000
- What do you think's going on?
- It's the attitude. The way people think.

234
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:18,700
The Great and Bountiful
Human Empire's stunted.

235
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:21,400
- How would you know?
- Trust me.

236
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:24,600
Humanity's been set back about 90 years.

237
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:28,100
When did Satellite Five start broadcasting?

238
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,100
91 years ago.

239
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:37,600
Mum, Dad, keep this message, OK?

240
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:42,300
<i>- Whatever you do, don't erase it.
-  Save it. You got that?</i>

241
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:44,400
OK.

242
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:52,500
The microprocessor became redundant
in the year 2019,

243
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:57,300
replaced by a system called SMT,
that's Single Molecule Transcription.

244
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:01,400
No, no, no! What are you doing? Come back!

245
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:05,700
Why are you doing that?

246
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:09,200
What's Floor 16? What's down there?

247
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:39,800
Sorry, um... Floor 16, that's, um...

248
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:43,100
- What do you cover?
- Medical non-emergency.

249
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:46,500
Wrong floor.
I'm having technical difficulties.

250
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:50,100
- My screen keeps locking me out.
- No, that's medical.

251
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:53,300
There must be something
wrong with your chip.

252
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:56,700
Yes. Yeah, of course, yeah.

253
00:22:57,900 --> 00:23:02,800
- I haven't got one.
- No wonder you can't get a screen to work.

254
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:07,500
- What are you? A... student?
- Yes.

255
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:12,100
Yeah, I'm... I'm on a research project

256
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:14,900
from the University of Mars.

257
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,400
- The Martian boondocks. Typical!
- Yep!

258
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:26,400
- Well, you still need chipping.
- So does that mean like brain surgery?

259
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:31,500
That's an old-fashioned phrase,
but it's the same thing, yes.

260
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,600
Oh, OK. Never mind.

261
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:39,200
But if I get a chip...
that means I could use any computer.

262
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,500
Absolutely.

263
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:44,300
You'll have to pay for it.

264
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,600
They've stopped subsidising.

265
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:51,400
Oh, right. Sorry.
Wasting your time. Thanks.

266
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,400
Hold on.

267
00:23:57,300 --> 00:23:59,400
Can I use this?

268
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:01,500
That'll do nicely.

269
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:04,600
It all comes down to two basic types.

270
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:10,900
Type one - the head chip - inserted
into the back of the skull. 100 credits.

271
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:15,600
There's the chip. Tiny. Invisible.

272
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:17,500
No scarring.

273
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,800
Type two is the full info-spike.

274
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:24,600
- Oh, that's the...
- thing.

275
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:28,900
That's the one. It does cost 10,000.

276
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:31,700
Oh, well, I couldn't afford it, then.

277
00:24:32,100 --> 00:24:33,600
Not at all.

278
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:37,300
It turns out you've got unlimited credit.

279
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:44,800
No, but I... I couldn't have it done.
I mean... that's got to hurt.

280
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:49,300
- Hasn't it?
- Painless. Contractual guarantee.

281
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:54,200
No, my mate's waiting upstairs.
I can't have major surgery.

282
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,100
It takes ten minutes.

283
00:24:57,400 --> 00:25:01,200
That sort of money buys a
very fast picosurgeon.

284
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:03,800
No, but I...

285
00:25:04,100 --> 00:25:06,900
I couldn't, though, no. It's...

286
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:12,500
Type one, you can interface
with a simple computer.

287
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:17,700
Type two, you ARE the computer.

288
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:23,100
You can transmit any piece of information
from the archive of Satellite Five,

289
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:27,400
which is just about the entire history
of the human race.

290
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,900
Now...

291
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:34,700
Which one's it going to be?

292
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:39,700
We're so gonna get in trouble!

293
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:46,500
- You're not allowed to touch the mainframe!
- Rose, tell her to button it.

294
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:49,700
If you vandalise the place, they'll notice!

295
00:25:51,100 --> 00:25:54,700
I don't understand.
We did a full security scan.

296
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:58,400
That man was there
when we found Suki Macrae Cantrell.

297
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:01,500
There were no indications about him.

298
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:04,200
And yet here he is...

299
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:08,000
clearly acting outside the parameters.

300
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:12,200
Fascinating!

301
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:15,400
Yes, sir.

302
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:19,300
Absolutely.

303
00:26:19,500 --> 00:26:21,100
At once!

304
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:25,100
Check him. Double-check him.
Triple-check him.

305
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:28,300
Quadruple.

306
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,900
- I'm going back to work.
- Go on, then. See you.

307
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:37,200
- I can't just leave you, can I?
- Get 'em to turn the heating down.

308
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:43,300
- It's boiling. Can't they do something about it?
- It's something to do with the turbine.

309
00:26:43,700 --> 00:26:47,300
- Something to do with the turbine (!)
- Well, I don't know!

310
00:26:47,700 --> 00:26:52,000
Exactly. I give up on you, Cathica.
Now, Rose asked the right question.

311
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:54,200
- I thank you.
- Why is it so hot?

312
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:58,900
- Why worry about the central heating?
- Never underestimate plumbing.

313
00:26:59,300 --> 00:27:01,500
Plumbing's very important.

314
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:08,500
<i>- Security scan complete.
- Well, who is he?</i>

315
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:10,900
<i>He is no one.</i>

316
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:13,700
What does that mean?

317
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:18,500
<i>- He is no one.
- What, you mean he has a fake ID?</i>

318
00:27:18,900 --> 00:27:21,300
<i>He has no identification.</i>

319
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:25,700
But everyone's registered.
We have a census for the entire Empire.

320
00:27:26,100 --> 00:27:28,900
<i>- He is no one.
- What, he doesn't exist?</i>

321
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,700
<i>- Not anywhere?
- He is no one.</i>

322
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,500
What about the blonde?

323
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:36,600
<i>- She is no one.
- Both of them?!</i>

324
00:27:36,900 --> 00:27:38,700
Well...

325
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:42,700
We all know what happens to non-entities.
They get promoted!

326
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:47,100
Bring 'em up.

327
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:51,800
Satellite Five - pipes and plumbing.
Look at the layout.

328
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:56,100
This is ridiculous.
You've got access to the computer's core.

329
00:27:56,400 --> 00:28:01,900
You could look at the archive, the stock
exchange... and you're looking at pipes?

330
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:04,100
But there's something wrong.

331
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:06,700
- I suppose...
- Why, what is it?

332
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:12,500
The ventilation system. Cooling ducts,
ice filters, all working flat out,

333
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:16,600
- channelling massive amounts of heat down.
- From the top.

334
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:20,800
- Floor 500.
- Something is generating tons of heat.

335
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:26,800
I feel like I'm missing out on a party.
It's all going on upstairs. Fancy a trip?

336
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:31,300
- You need a key.
- Keys are just codes. I've got them right here.

337
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:35,900
Here we go. Override 215.9.

338
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:42,500
- How come it gave YOU the code?
- Someone up there likes me.

339
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,400
I told you it was painless.

340
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:55,500
No scarring, you see?

341
00:28:56,900 --> 00:28:58,800
Perfect success.

342
00:28:59,900 --> 00:29:01,800
How do I activate it?

343
00:29:02,100 --> 00:29:04,100
It's a personal choice.

344
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,900
Some people whistle.

345
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:10,400
I know one man who triggers it
with "Oh, Danny Boy".

346
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:15,700
You're set on default for now.
That's a click of the fingers.

347
00:29:16,100 --> 00:29:18,500
So, you mean I just?

348
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,000
Click.

349
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:27,700
- Come with us.
- No way.

350
00:29:27,900 --> 00:29:31,000
- Bye!
- Well, don't mention my name.

351
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:34,100
When you get in trouble, don't involve me.

352
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:38,000
That's her gone. Adam's given up.
It's just you and me.

353
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:40,200
- Yeah.
- Good.

354
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:41,800
Yep.

355
00:29:56,700 --> 00:29:58,900
Oh, my God! I'm going to be sick.

356
00:30:08,500 --> 00:30:09,800
Special offer.

357
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:15,600
We installed the vomit-o-matic too.
Nano-termites are in the lining of your throat.

358
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,100
In the event of sickness...

359
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:21,100
they freeze the waste.

360
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
The walls are not made of gold.

361
00:30:37,100 --> 00:30:39,100
You should go back downstairs.

362
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:41,300
Tough!

363
00:30:58,500 --> 00:31:00,800
I started without you.

364
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:05,800
This is fascinating! Satellite Five
contains every piece of information

365
00:31:06,300 --> 00:31:09,500
within the Fourth Great and Bountiful
Human Empire...

366
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:15,700
birth certificates, shopping habits, bank
statements - but you two, you don't exist.

367
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:19,200
- There's not a trace.
- No birth. No job.

368
00:31:19,500 --> 00:31:23,100
Not the slightest kiss.
How can you walk through the world

369
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:25,600
and not leave a single footprint?

370
00:31:25,900 --> 00:31:27,800
Suki!

371
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:31,000
Hello? Can you hear me?

372
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:33,400
Suki! What have you done to her?

373
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:35,900
I think she's dead.

374
00:31:37,900 --> 00:31:42,000
- She's working.
- The chips in their head keep going.

375
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:45,500
- Like puppets.
- Oh! You're full of information!

376
00:31:45,900 --> 00:31:51,200
It's only fair we get some information back
because, apparently, you're no one.

377
00:31:51,500 --> 00:31:55,300
It's so rare not to know something.
Who are you?

378
00:31:55,700 --> 00:31:59,500
It doesn't matter 'cause we're off.
Nice to meet you. Come on.

379
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:07,100
- Tell me who you are.
- That fact is keeping us alive. I won't say.

380
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:10,700
My Editor-in-chief
might convince you otherwise.

381
00:32:10,900 --> 00:32:12,400
And who's that?

382
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:19,900
It may interest you to know that this is not
the Fourth Great and Bountiful Human Empire.

383
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:24,900
It's not human at all! It's merely
a place where humans happen to live.

384
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:28,400
Yeah.

385
00:32:28,700 --> 00:32:31,500
Yep. Sorry.

386
00:32:31,900 --> 00:32:37,500
It's a place where humans are allowed to
live by kind permission of my client.

387
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:53,600
- What is that?
- That thing's in charge of Satellite Five?

388
00:32:53,900 --> 00:32:58,500
That thing, as you put it,
is in charge of the human race.

389
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:04,800
For almost 100 years, mankind's behaviour
has been controlled by its broadcast news,

390
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:07,100
edited by my superior,

391
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:08,700
your master

392
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:15,500
and humanity's guiding light, the Mighty
Jagrafess of the Holy Hadrojassic Maxarodenfoe.

393
00:33:16,800 --> 00:33:18,100
I call him Max.

394
00:33:56,100 --> 00:34:00,100
Create a climate of fear
and it's easy to keep the borders closed.

395
00:34:00,500 --> 00:34:06,500
It's just a matter of emphasis. The right word
in the right broadcast repeated often enough

396
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:10,500
can destabilise an economy,
invent an enemy, change a vote.

397
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:13,500
So all the people on Earth are like slaves?

398
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:16,800
Well, now, there's an interesting point.

399
00:34:17,200 --> 00:34:21,000
Is a slave a slave
if he doesn't know he's enslaved?

400
00:34:21,300 --> 00:34:24,500
- Yes.
- Oh! I was hoping for a philosophical debate.

401
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:27,400
- Is that all I'm going to get. "Yes"?
- Yes.

402
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:29,200
You're no fun.

403
00:34:29,500 --> 00:34:32,500
Undo these.
You'll find out how much fun I am.

404
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:34,800
Ooh, he's tough, isn't he?

405
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:39,400
But come on. Isn't it a great system?
You've got to admire it a little bit.

406
00:34:39,800 --> 00:34:42,700
You can't hide this.
Someone must have noticed.

407
00:34:43,900 --> 00:34:49,700
From time to time, yes, but the computer chip
system allows me to see inside their brains.

408
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,800
I can see the smallest
doubt, then crush it.

409
00:35:09,300 --> 00:35:14,600
Then they just carry on,
living the life, strutting about downstairs

410
00:35:14,900 --> 00:35:20,300
and all over the Earth like they're so individual
when they're not - they're just cattle.

411
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:24,300
In that respect,
the Jagrafess hasn't changed a thing.

412
00:35:24,500 --> 00:35:28,800
- What about you? You're not a Jagrabelly thing.
- Jagrafess.

413
00:35:29,100 --> 00:35:34,500
- You're not a Jagrafess. You're human.
- Simply being human doesn't pay very well.

414
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:38,800
- You couldn't have done this on your own.
- No!

415
00:35:39,100 --> 00:35:41,600
I represent a consortium of banks.

416
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:44,500
Money prefers a long-term investment.

417
00:35:44,700 --> 00:35:48,500
Also, the Jagrafess needed a hand
to install himself.

418
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:50,900
No wonder. He's big.

419
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:53,500
- What's his lifespan?
- 3,000 years.

420
00:35:53,700 --> 00:35:59,100
- That's a huge metabolism generating heat.
- That's why Satellite Five's so hot.

421
00:35:59,500 --> 00:36:04,700
You pump it out of the creature, channel it
downstairs. Jagrafess stays cool and alive.

422
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:07,900
Satellite Five is a life-support system.

423
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:16,400
<i>- It's me again.
- Don't wipe this message.</i>

424
00:36:16,700 --> 00:36:21,800
It's just going to sound like white noise,
but save it 'cause I can translate it, OK?

425
00:36:25,200 --> 00:36:30,500
Three, two, one... and spike.

426
00:36:35,100 --> 00:36:37,700
But that's why you're so dangerous.

427
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:41,600
Knowledge is power, but you remain unknown.

428
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:44,700
Who are you?

429
00:36:53,900 --> 00:36:58,000
Leave her alone. I'm the Doctor,
she's Rose Tyler. We're nothing.

430
00:36:58,300 --> 00:36:59,800
Tell me who you are.

431
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:02,400
- I just said.
- Who do you work for?

432
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:06,200
Who sent you? Who knows about us?
Who exactly?

433
00:37:06,500 --> 00:37:08,100
Agh!

434
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:12,500
Time Lord!

435
00:37:14,300 --> 00:37:16,200
- What?
- Oh, yes!

436
00:37:16,500 --> 00:37:20,400
The last of the Time Lords
and his travelling machine.

437
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:25,800
- With his little human girl from long ago.
- What are you talking about?

438
00:37:26,100 --> 00:37:27,500
Time travel.

439
00:37:28,700 --> 00:37:30,700
Agh!

440
00:37:30,900 --> 00:37:32,300
Help!

441
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:35,000
Someone's been telling you lies.

442
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:38,000
Young Master Adam Mitchell?

443
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:42,400
<i>Help! Agh!</i>

444
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,400
Oh, my God, his head!

445
00:37:45,700 --> 00:37:48,000
What the hell's he done?

446
00:37:48,900 --> 00:37:52,200
What the hell's he done?
They're reading his mind.

447
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:56,400
- He's telling them everything.
- I know everything about you.

448
00:37:56,700 --> 00:38:00,300
Every piece of information in his head
is now mine.

449
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:03,500
And you have infinite knowledge, Doctor.

450
00:38:03,800 --> 00:38:10,400
The Human Empire is tiny compared to what
you've seen in your T-A-R-D-I-S. Tardis.

451
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:15,500
- You'll never get that. I'll die first.
- Die all you like. I've got the key.

452
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:30,400
- You and your boyfriends!
- Today, WE are the headlines.

453
00:38:30,700 --> 00:38:34,900
We can rewrite history.
We could prevent mankind from developing.

454
00:38:35,300 --> 00:38:40,700
No one will stop you because you've bred
a human race which doesn't ask questions.

455
00:38:41,100 --> 00:38:43,800
Stupid little slaves believing every lie.

456
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:49,200
They'll trot right into the slaughterhouse
if they're told it's made of gold.

457
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:05,700
Disengage safety.

458
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:11,600
What's happening?

459
00:39:13,200 --> 00:39:16,600
Maximum access. Override floor 139.

460
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:22,400
And spike!

461
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,600
Someone's disengaged the safety.

462
00:39:27,900 --> 00:39:29,500
Who's that?

463
00:39:34,700 --> 00:39:38,500
- It's Cathica!
- She's thinking. She's using what she knows!

464
00:39:38,900 --> 00:39:40,600
Terminate her access!

465
00:39:40,900 --> 00:39:45,500
Everything I told her about the pipes,
the filters - she's reversing it.

466
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,900
Look at that! It's getting hot.

467
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,800
I said terminate her!

468
00:39:54,100 --> 00:39:56,100
Burn out her mind!

469
00:39:57,500 --> 00:40:01,800
Oh, no, you don't.
You should have promoted me years back!

470
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:33,100
She's venting the heat up here. The Jagrafess has
to stay cool - now it's on top of a volcano!

471
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:40,500
Yes, I'm trying, sir, but...

472
00:40:40,800 --> 00:40:45,200
It's impossible -
a member of staff with an idea!

473
00:40:53,500 --> 00:40:55,700
- What do I do?
- Flick the switch!

474
00:41:12,700 --> 00:41:15,000
Oi! Do you want to bank on a certainty?

475
00:41:15,300 --> 00:41:18,800
Massive heat in a massive body -
massive bang!

476
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:21,200
See you in the headlines!

477
00:41:26,700 --> 00:41:30,100
If it's all the same to you,
I think I'll resign. Bye.

478
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,700
Let go of me!

479
00:41:44,600 --> 00:41:46,200
Let go of me!

480
00:41:46,500 --> 00:41:48,200
Let go of me!

481
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:54,700
Agh!

482
00:42:11,800 --> 00:42:15,000
We're gonna go. Too many questions.
You'll manage.

483
00:42:15,300 --> 00:42:19,300
- No one will believe me.
- They might believe a lot of things now.

484
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:23,200
- Humans will get back to normal.
- What about your friend?

485
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,800
He's not my friend.

486
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:30,800
- Now, don't...
- I'm all right now.

487
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:33,100
Much better. And I've got the key.

488
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:34,900
Look, it's...

489
00:42:35,900 --> 00:42:38,700
It all worked out for the best, didn't it?

490
00:42:40,100 --> 00:42:44,900
You know, it's not actually my fault
because you were in charge...

491
00:42:47,300 --> 00:42:49,300
This is my house! I'm home.

492
00:42:49,500 --> 00:42:54,900
Oh, my God, I'm home! Blimey!
I thought you were going to chuck me out of an airlock.

493
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:59,300
- Is there something else you want to tell me?
- No. What do you mean?

494
00:43:01,300 --> 00:43:06,600
The archive of Satellite Five.
One second of that message could have changed the world.

495
00:43:14,300 --> 00:43:17,700
- That's it, then. See you.
- How do you mean, see you?

496
00:43:18,100 --> 00:43:21,600
- As in goodbye.
- What about me? You can't just go.

497
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:24,800
- I have a chip type two. My head opens.
- Like this?

498
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:29,000
- Don't.
- Don't do what?

499
00:43:30,500 --> 00:43:32,500
Stop it!

500
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:35,000
All right, that's enough. Stop it.

501
00:43:37,900 --> 00:43:39,400
Thank you.

502
00:43:39,500 --> 00:43:41,600
- Oi!
- Sorry. I couldn't resist.

503
00:43:41,900 --> 00:43:45,900
- History could have changed because of you.
- I just wanted to help.

504
00:43:46,300 --> 00:43:49,800
- You were helping yourself.
- I said I'm sorry, and I am.

505
00:43:50,200 --> 00:43:52,400
You can't just leave me like this.

506
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:58,100
If anyone sees that head, they'll dissect you in seconds.
You'll have to lead a quiet life.

507
00:43:58,500 --> 00:44:00,700
Be average. Unseen. Good luck.

508
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:03,200
But I want to come with you.

509
00:44:03,500 --> 00:44:06,900
I only take the best. I've got Rose.

510
00:44:07,700 --> 00:44:09,200
Rose!

511
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:13,300
- Oh, my God!
- Who's that? Geoff, is that you?

512
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:17,400
- It's me, Mum. Don't come in. Wait there.
- Oh, my Lord!

513
00:44:17,800 --> 00:44:20,000
You never said you were coming home!

514
00:44:21,100 --> 00:44:23,700
Hold on. I'll just take my coat off.

515
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Rose, take me with you.

516
00:44:29,800 --> 00:44:32,000
What's that noise?

517
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:36,100
Have you left the back door open?
Blimey, there's a draught!

518
00:44:36,500 --> 00:44:40,300
What a surprise! Let me look at you!

519
00:44:40,600 --> 00:44:42,700
Six months!

520
00:44:42,900 --> 00:44:47,200
It's like I saw you yesterday.
Time goes by like that.

521
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:56,400
Be careful what you wish for.

522
00:44:56,700 --> 00:45:00,900
The day my father died.
It's just an ordinary day.

523
00:45:01,300 --> 00:45:04,500
Oh, God, this is it.
He can't die on his own!

524
00:45:05,900 --> 00:45:08,200
Can I try again?

525
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:11,800
- Oh, God, this is it.
- Rose, no!

526
00:45:14,100 --> 00:45:17,700
- I chose another stupid ape!
- I haven't changed history.

527
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:23,300
A man is alive who wasn't alive before.
The world's different because he's alive.

528
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:29,600
Time's been damaged.
They've come to sterilise the wound.

529
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:31,800
- Get in the church!
- Agh!
